== Damage Scaling ==
Damage scaling is a mechanic introduced in [[The Binding of Isaac: Afterbirth]] to provide a more challenging experience to players, enabling ''some'' enemies to retaliate against high damage attacks by deploying an "armor" of a sort to greatly reduce the amount of damage taken. Further details and an in-depth explanation may be found [[Damage Scaling|here]].

== Trivia ==
* Ultra Death, like the other Ultra Harbingers is an upgraded version of his regular counterpart, {{e|Death}}.
** Unlike the others, he has the greatest variation in behavior from regular Death- notably the lack of a second phase where he dismounts, while each of the Ultra Harbingers share their specific second phase transiton with their regular counterpart. (Famine losing everything except their head, Pestilence only losing their head and War losing their horse)
**The visual similarity of Ultra Death's horse and a scythe, which the regular counterpart has, is made more apparent with the body of Ultra Death's horse having a curve (like farming scythes have) and sharing the same wood texture & colour as the handle of Ultra Death's scythe. 
* The violin heard in the section of Revelations 13:1 that plays during Ultra Death's fight is performed by Carla Kihlstedt, the voice actor for {{e|Mom}}.
* Ultra Death can be seen facepalming in the background after killing {{e|Ultra War}}.
* The wave of Ultra Death Heads loosely resembles one of {{e|Conquest}}'s attack.
** This could be compensation for Conquest's lack of appearance despite his [[Harbinger]] role.
* Ultra Death's glowing eye during the darkness attack could be a reference to the ''[[Wikipedia:Terminator (franchise)|Terminator]]'' series, as Ultra Death bears some resemblance to the Terminators seen in those movies.
* Ultra Death's glowing eye is actually invisible during the whole fight but active the whole time, and becomes visible when the room is darkened. Using {{p|XIX - The Sun?}} darkens the arena, making it visible.
* Ultra Death is male.

